      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the `start_oauth_login.py` file that starts an OAuth or OIDC authorization-code login, I need to choose a concrete external provider and make it identifiable in the code. I will use the Google OAuth 2.0 provider for this task, as it is a widely used and well-documented service. I will import the necessary modules from the `google-auth` library, which is the official Python client library for Google's discovery-based APIs. This will make the provider identifiable in the code. </thinking>\n",
